              "text": "sarmâ khordan pairs sarmâ, \"the cold\" (from sard, \"cold\", inherited, EtymDB), with khordan, \"to eat\": to \"eat\" the cold, the way Persian also \"eats\" a blow or a fall. khordan, \"to eat\", is an inherited verb; EtymDB traces it to Middle Persian xwar-, \"to eat\"."
